  m_Name: 829d6704-c357-4fcc-874c-5df5b896602f
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _text: "Report on Disciplinary Actions\r\nTo: [Human Resources Department]\r\n\r\n\r\nSubject:
    Disciplinary Actions and Reasons\r\nThe following report outlines the disciplinary
    actions taken against employees for various infractions, in accordance with company
    policy and the standards of conduct expected within our organization.\r\nEmployee:
    Jo\xE3o Silva Monteiro\r\nPunishment: Written Warning\r\nReason: Not adhering
    to the company's designated prayer times.\r\nEmployee: Maria Oliveira dos Santos\r\nPunishment:
    Suspension (1 week)\r\nReason: Neglecting the tithe contributions to the Church
    of Light.\r\nEmployee: Carlos Souza Almeida\r\nPunishment: Written Warning\r\nReason:
    Use of sick days near a deadline.\r\nEmployee: Ana Pereira Faria Lima\r\nPunishment:
    Written Warning\r\nReason: Not participating in daily prayer sessions.\r\nEmployee:
    Bruno Santos de Vasconcelos\r\nPunishment: Suspension (2 weeks)\r\nReason: Failing
    to meet the mandatory tithe requirement for three consecutive months.\r\nEmployee:
    Fernanda Costa Magalh\xE3es\r\nPunishment: Termination of Employment\r\nReason:
    Following a heretic religion, contrary to the principles of the Church of Light.*\r\nEmployee:
    Pedro Lima Costa de Souza\r\nPunishment: Verbal Warning\r\nReason: Neglecting
    participation in communal prayer activities.\r\nEmployee: Camila Almeida Prado\r\nPunishment:
    Written Warning\r\nReason: Failing to observe prayer times and disrupting the
    spiritual harmony of the workplace.\r\nEmployee: Rafael Barbosa da Silva Santos\r\nPunishment:
    Suspension (1 week)\r\nReason: Unauthorized absence and excessive use of sick
    days.\r\nEmployee: Patr\xEDcia Gomes Albuquerque Ferreira\r\nPunishment: Termination
    of Employment\r\nReason: Repeatedly neglecting the tithe and failing to adhere
    to prayer practices, despite prior warnings.\r\n*Former employee also reported
    to the Apostolic Authorities.\r\n\r\nThese disciplinary measures have been implemented
    to maintain the integrity of our workplace practices and uphold the values we
    cherish. All actions taken are in strict compliance with our internal policies
    and the guidance of the Church of Light.\r\nRespectfully submitted,\r\n[Bex Eliana
    M\xFCller]\r\n[Overseer and General Manager]"
  _nodeType: 3
  _isRootNode: 0
